<HR size="1" color="#003366">
<FONT SIZE="2" FACE="Verdana, Helvetica, sans-serif">
During official guild raids we expect everyone to follow these rules: <BR><UL TYPE=SQUARE>1. - Be on time at the designated time and place that is set for the raid. Either camp your character at the designated place the night before or get on early to make sure you get a ride. If you are not there at the start time, you will not be ensured a spot in a group. <P>2. - If you know that you will be late, speak with the raid leader to make arrangements. If you do not make arrangements to arrive late, we will not wait and you will have to get there yourself or just be patient. No Whining Allowed. <P>3. - Have any equipment or resist gear that is needed on you at the appointed time. We don't want to hear people asking to borrow gear, have to run to the bank, or have jewelry made for them at the last minute. It's your responsibility to be prepared ahead of time. <P>4. - It is highly recommended that everyone have several small coffins on them. <P>5. - Tanks should have a gate potion or two on them for raids such as Hate/PoF/PoG, etc. <P>6. - No one invites other people from outside the guild along unless you clear it with the Raid Leader first. New members on probation aren't allowed to invite guests on guild raids. <P>7. - If a situation arises where there's a problem during a raid with another guild or individuals outside the guild let the officers deal with it. <A HREF="http://www.vallisscortor.com/UBB/cgi-bin/ultimatebb.cgi?ubb=get_topic&f=12&t=000002" TARGET=_blank><B>See Communications Rules</B></A><P>8. - We expect everyone to conduct him or herself in a respectable manner and not inflame a situation by shouts or OOC talk or tells to the individuals we're having a conflict with. <A HREF="http://www.vallisscortor.com/UBB/cgi-bin/ultimatebb.cgi?ubb=get_topic&f=12&t=000002" TARGET=_blank><B>See Communications Rules</B></A><P>9. - All members must respect whatever decisions or compromises the officers come up with. If you have a problem with that discuss it AFTER the raid please. These situations are usually difficult at best and not made easier with people yelling at each other. <P>10. - Once a raid has started the organizers will make groups and keep you informed on tactics & important orders. We expect everyone to listen. We realize sometimes people are zoning or miss their group list so these orders will be repeated. At this point please control jokes, horsing around, repeated emotes. This helps not only the organizers but also everyone else who's trying to pay attention. Feel free to relax and mess around before or after a raid but once we're in Fight Mode please try to control yourselves. <P>11. - The Raid Leader or the person assigned to make the groups will list the group leader first in a grouping list. Please do not argue with them about whom you're grouped with. Each group leader is responsible for letting the Raid Leader know the status of their group, mana status, rez status, LD status, lost corpses, etc. - any important information will be relayed to the Raid Leader by EACH group leader. If the group leader goes LD on a raid the remaining members will regroup ASAP and that new group leader will relay their status to the Raid Leader. <P>12. - No Dueling without permission from guild leader or raid leader. <P>13. - Do not question guild leader or raid leader’s decisions during guild events. If you have questions, suggestions, or comments about any decisions, or people, please contact officers or guild leader ‘AFTER’ guild events. <P>14. - Members are requested to attend guild events if you are online and of appropriate level during those events or if your assistance is requested. If you have more than 1 suitable character for the guild event, consult your guild leader or raid leader about which char you should bring to guild events. Remember that every member is needed at guild events. If you are not needed in the guild, you shouldn’t be in the guild in the first place. <P>15. - Do not wander/gate/evacuate/camp/zone/leave camp without guild leader or raid leader’s permission. This includes running to get puller’s corpse and/or pulling. This also includes leaving early in guild events to play twinks somewhere else <B>(refer to rule#12)</B>. <P>16. - Do not give out commands in guild events in any way. Only guild leader and raid leader can make such decision. Only authorized puller can issue a moving command. Again, if guild leader and raid leader are AFK, officers will be in charge. <P>17. - All rare gems, normal gems, treasures looted during guild event period should go to guild banker. If guild banker is not around, please hand them to officers or guild leader at the end of the raid. Once we pay for raid, we will lotto. See Loot rules<P>18. - If you acquire an item from a guild event, you must turn in your old item of the same type (e.g.: Crystalline Short Sword vs. Lamentation Blade), unless your old item is still useful to you at some point (e.g.: Bone caster robe vs. Haste robe). This ONLY applies to items awarded to you from the guild, not items you got on your own time. <P>19. - Nobody loots <B>ANYTHING</B> without officer's/Raid leader's permission even if they think it will rot. <A HREF="http://www.vallisscortor.com/UBB/cgi-bin/ultimatebb.cgi?ubb=get_topic&f=11&t=000002" TARGET=_blank><B>See Loot Rules.</B></A></UL><P>Signed by the High Council:<BR>Nitrain, Sorack, Santerre, Bobbib, Larlaana, Artallen
</FONT>
